# Denylist for tools/check-public-safe.sh — one term per line, case-insensitive
# substring match. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# COPY THIS TO tools/.pii-terms AND FILL IT IN. That file is gitignored on
# purpose: a list of someone's medications and symptoms is itself the personal
# data we are trying to keep out of the repo, so it must never be committed.
#
# What belongs in it — anything that would identify one person's health picture
# if a stranger read this repo:
#
#   - medication and supplement names in the user's stack
#   - condition and symptom names, including abbreviations
#   - the user's private vocabulary for a sensation or routine
#   - device model names, clinician or facility names, place names
#   - household details that recur in observations (people, pets, rooms)
#
# What does NOT belong in it — generic clinical vocabulary the skills legitimately
# need: "heart rate", "stress", "sleep", "blood pressure", "symptom", "dose".
#
# Example shape (replace entirely):
# <medication-name>
# <supplement-name>
# <condition-abbreviation>
# <private-term-for-a-symptom>
# <device-model>
